# SEO Content Writing Rules

When editing copy in `src/data/` or homepage / page components:

## Required shape

- **Titles**: `{Game} {Page} | {Brand}` — under ~60 characters
- **Descriptions**: one clear benefit + platform; under ~160 characters
- **Body**: short paragraphs; lists over walls of text
- **Internal links**: use nav labels (Features, Store, Status, FAQ) — few, purposeful

## Homepage

- Hero: brand name + one short line + Buy CTA
- Categories: Features / Status / Store / Help — short link labels only
- FAQ: simple questions employees would ask before buying

## Rebrand checklist (copy)

1. Edit `src/data/brand.ts` (name, url, game, keywords, plans) → `npm run sync:brand`
2. Rewrite EN simple pages + FAQs with `{brand}` / `{game}` tokens
3. Keep section count and heading style the same
4. Keep “simple English” — no denser copy for “more SEO”
5. Do not hardcode the old brand in Hero, footer, reviews, or 404

## Forbidden

- Rewriting pages into long SEO essays
- Adding keyword piles in H1s
- Changing URL architecture without an explicit product decision
- Scraping third-party site images for SEO assets
